# Raw captures from this pass — deliberately NOT committed.
#
# The 69-key public config is unauthenticated and carries credential-shaped values
# (a reCAPTCHA site key, and an x-api-key under each of the two `nutrino.cc.*`
# service keys). docs/04-configuration.md holds the cross-deployment comparison of
# those back for a disclosure decision, so this repo publishes none of the values.
#
# Committing docs/*.json would therefore put credentials in the diff. The
# committable form of this pass is the REDACTION, not the capture:
#
#   probe.sh            what was requested, one line per request (no bodies)
#   requests.tsv        method / host / path / status / bytes / content-type
#   enumerate.py        the enumeration itself — re-runnable, so the searched
#                       key list is auditable without the raw bytes
#   scrub.py            redacts a capture into a committable extract
#   enumeration-scrubbed.txt   the full enumeration, values replaced by typed
#                       placeholders and self-checked against scrub-patterns.txt
#   credential-shapes.py / .txt   key paths, lengths and character-class shapes
#                       only; no value is printed, hashed or compared
#
# To re-derive: bash probe.sh && python3 enumerate.py > enumeration.txt \
#               && python3 scrub.py enumeration.txt enumeration-scrubbed.txt
docs/
enumeration.txt